The user wants to create a Google Cloud EC2 instance? Actually EC2 is AWS. In GCP it's Compute Engine. They want an instance with RTX A6000 GPU and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS. We need to provide API call. Likely use gcloud compute instances create command. Provide JSON body for REST API. Use gcloud CLI? Provide REST API endpoint: POST https://compute.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/{project}/zones/{zone}/instances. Body includes machineType, disks, guestAccelerators, etc.

We can give example using curl. Provide placeholders for project, zone, instanceName. Also specify GPU type: nvidia-tesla-a6000. Need to enable GPUs. Also need to set preemptible? Not necessary.

Also need to add service account, scopes, network interface. Provide minimal config.

Let's craft:

curl -X POST \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $(gcloud auth application-default print-access-token)" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d @instance.json \
  "https://compute.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/${PROJECT_ID}/zones/${ZONE}/instances"

